    "issue_alignment": "The ZMTP/1.0 v1 decoder uses the fixed c_single_allocator, whose buffer is needlessly resized by decoder_base_t::resize_buffer() after every socket read (stream_engine_base_t::in_event_internal). Unlike the shared_message_memory_allocator (used by v2/v3 decoders), the static allocator's buffer cannot grow; resize() only inflates the reported size, so a large message body (>8192 bytes received in one read) makes the next get_buffer()/read() overflow the fixed 8192-byte buffer."
